# Shell scripts must keep LF endings whatever the host git is configured to do.
# Git on Windows checks out CRLF by default, and bash in the Linux container then
# treats the trailing \r as part of the last token on each line. Verified failures
# without this file, on a checkout made with core.autocrlf=true:
#
#   .devcontainer/welcome.sh        syntax error: unexpected end of file
#                                   (runs on every attach via postAttachCommand)
#   infra/generate-sas-tokens.sh    set: pipefail: invalid option name
#                                   (dies on line 9, before doing anything)
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Notebooks are JSON; normalising them is fine and keeps diffs sane.
*.ipynb text eol=lf

# The committed synthetic dataset. Never touch these.
*.parquet binary
